{
  "name": "MARKAI - Unified Publisher",
  "description": "MARKAI unified publisher. RE-IMPORT REQUIRED after the 2026-08-21 webhook-hardening backend deploy: callbacks now echo the dispatch's X-Webhook-Event-Id (replay dedup) and send a body-bound HMAC signature (X-Webhook-Signature = 'sha256=' + hex(hmac_sha256(secret, timestamp + '.' + raw_body)), with X-Webhook-Timestamp in unix seconds) computed in Code nodes. Operator setup: (1) set N8N_WEBHOOK_HMAC_SECRET in the n8n environment to the SAME value as the backend's N8N_WEBHOOK_HMAC_SECRET, (2) set NODE_FUNCTION_ALLOW_BUILTIN=crypto so the Code nodes can require('crypto'), (3) re-import this workflow. Until the HMAC secret is set on BOTH sides the backend accepts the legacy static-secret path (deprecated, logged). The backend also now always sends X-Webhook-Secret on dispatch — a first-node secret check against $env.N8N_WEBHOOK_SECRET can (and should) be added to reject foreign calls.",
